From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Anze <aanzdev@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 4 Jun 2026 14:55:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] usb: dwc3: SM8750 force USB power-off on host system suspend

On SM8750 (AYN Odin 3), suspending to deep with a USB host device/dock
attached hard-hangs the SoC: every kernel suspend phase completes
(verified with pm_test: devices+core resume, only pm_test=none hangs),
so the failure is the firmware power-collapse refusing to drop the USB
power island. Stock Android (downstream msm-dwc3) avoids this by fully
powering USB down before sleep; mainline dwc3-qcom instead KEEPS the
eUSB2/QMP PHYs powered whenever the controller is wakeup-capable
(device_may_wakeup() goes true once the dock's HID devices enable remote
wakeup), taking the phy_pm_runtime_put_sync() path in dwc3_suspend_common()
rather than dwc3_core_exit(). That leaves the PHYs up and wedges the
collapse.

This handheld never needs USB to wake the system (the power button does),
so force the full power-off path for host-mode *system* (non-auto) suspend:
always dwc3_core_exit()/dwc3_core_init_for_resume(), and tell the qcom glue
to treat USB as non-wakeup so it does not arm the HS-PHY wake IRQs or keep
clocks/PHYs alive. Runtime PM is unaffected.

--- a/drivers/usb/dwc3/core.c
+++ b/drivers/usb/dwc3/core.c
@@ -2502,8 +2502,16 @@
 		dwc3_core_exit(dwc);
 		break;
 	case DWC3_GCTL_PRTCAP_HOST:
-		if (!PMSG_IS_AUTO(msg) &&
-		    (!device_may_wakeup(dwc->dev) || dwc->needs_full_reinit)) {
+		/*
+		 * ROCKNIX/SM8750: with a USB host device attached, keeping the
+		 * eUSB2/QMP PHYs powered for remote-wakeup leaves the USB power
+		 * island up and wedges the SoC deep-suspend power-collapse
+		 * (every kernel suspend phase completes; only the firmware sleep
+		 * entry hangs - confirmed via pm_test). Force the full power-off
+		 * path on system suspend so the PHYs are powered down; USB cannot
+		 * wake the system (the power button does), which is fine here.
+		 */
+		if (!PMSG_IS_AUTO(msg)) {
 			dwc3_core_exit(dwc);
 			break;
 		}
@@ -2566,8 +2574,8 @@
 		dwc3_gadget_resume(dwc);
 		break;
 	case DWC3_GCTL_PRTCAP_HOST:
-		if (!PMSG_IS_AUTO(msg) &&
-		    (!device_may_wakeup(dwc->dev) || dwc->needs_full_reinit)) {
+		/* ROCKNIX/SM8750: match the forced full power-off on suspend. */
+		if (!PMSG_IS_AUTO(msg)) {
 			ret = dwc3_core_init_for_resume(dwc);
 			if (ret)
 				return ret;
--- a/drivers/usb/dwc3/dwc3-qcom.c
+++ b/drivers/usb/dwc3/dwc3-qcom.c
@@ -749,7 +749,13 @@
 {
 	struct dwc3 *dwc = dev_get_drvdata(dev);
 	struct dwc3_qcom *qcom = to_dwc3_qcom(dwc);
-	bool wakeup = device_may_wakeup(dev);
+	/*
+	 * ROCKNIX/SM8750: do not keep USB armed as a system wakeup source.
+	 * Pairing with the forced core power-off in dwc3_suspend_common(),
+	 * this guarantees the USB power island is fully down so the SoC can
+	 * reach deep low-power with a host/dock attached.
+	 */
+	bool wakeup = false;
 	int ret;
 
 	ret = dwc3_pm_suspend(&qcom->dwc);
@@ -769,7 +775,8 @@
 {
 	struct dwc3 *dwc = dev_get_drvdata(dev);
 	struct dwc3_qcom *qcom = to_dwc3_qcom(dwc);
-	bool wakeup = device_may_wakeup(dev);
+	/* ROCKNIX/SM8750: match dwc3_qcom_pm_suspend() - USB not a wake source. */
+	bool wakeup = false;
 	int ret;
 
 	ret = dwc3_qcom_resume(qcom, wakeup);
